item-meta {\n   133→            font-size: 8pt;\n   134→            color: #828282;\n   135→        }\n   136→\n   137→        .item-meta a {\n   138→            color: #828282;\n   139→        }\n   140→\n   141→        .item-meta a:hover {\n   142→            color: #000000;\n   143→        }\n   144→\n   145→        .tag {\n   146→            display: inline-block;\n   147→            background-color: #f0f0f0;\n   148→            padding: 1px 4px;\n   149→            border-radius: 2px;\n   150→            font-size: 8pt;\n   151→            margin-right: 4px;\n   152→            margin-top: 4px;\n   153→        }\n   154→\n   155→        .quote {\n   156→            background-color: #f9f9f9;\n   157→            border-left: 3px solid #ff6600;\n   158→            padding: 6px 8px;\n   159→            margin: 6px 0;\n   160→            font-size: 9pt;\n   161→            color: #555555;\n   162→            font-style: italic;\n   163→            line-height: 1.4;\n   164→        }\n   165→\n   166→        .update-type {\n   167→            display: inline-block;\n   168→            padding: 2px 6px;\n   169→            border-radius: 2px;\n   170→            font-size: 8pt;\n   171→            font-weight: bold;\n   172→            margin-bottom: 4px;\n   173→        }\n   174→\n   175→        .update-type.release {\n   176→            background-color: #e6f7ff;\n   177→            color: #0066cc;\n   178→        }\n   179→\n   180→        .update-type.feature {\n   181→            background-color: #f6ffed;\n   182→            color: #52c41a;\n   183→        }\n   184→\n   185→        .update-type.announcement {\n   186→            background-color: #fff7e6;\n   187→            color: #fa8c16;\n   188→        }\n   189→\n   190→        .topics {\n   191→            margin-top: 4px;\n   192→        }\n   193→\n   194→        .footer {\n   195→            max-width: 1200px;\n   196→            margin: 20px auto 0;\n   197→            padding: 10px 6px;\n   198→            border-top: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n   199→            text-align: center;\n   200→            font-size: 9pt;\n   201→            color: #828282;\n   202→        }\n   203→\n   204→        .footer a {\n   205→            color: #828282;\n   206→            margin: 0 10px;\n   207→        }\n   208→\n   209→        .footer a:hover {\n   210→            color: #000000;\n   211→        }\n   212→\n   213→        .section-count {\n   214→            font-size: 8pt;\n   215→            color: #828282;\n   216→            font-weight: normal;\n   217→            margin-left: 5px;\n   218→        }\n   219→\n   220→        @media (max-width: 900px) {\n   221→            .three-column-layout {\n   222→                grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n   223→            }\n   224→        }\n   225→\n   226→        @media print {\n   227→            body {\n   228→                background-color: #ffffff;\n   229→            }\n   230→\n   231→            .column {\n   232→                border: 1px solid #000000;\n   233→                page-break-inside: avoid;\n   234→            }\n   235→\n   236→            .column-header {\n   237→                background-color: #eeeeee !important;\n   238→                -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;\n   239→                print-color-adjust: exact;\n   240→            }\n   241→\n   242→            a {\n   243→                color: #000000 !important;\n   244→                text-decoration: underline;\n   245→            }\n   246→\n   247→            .item {\n   248→                page-break-inside: avoid;\n   249→            }\n   250→        }\n   251→    </style>\n   252→</head>\n   253→<body>\n   254→    <header class=\"header\">\n   255→        <div class=\"header-content\">\n   256→            <h1>Agentic Coding Research Report</h1>\n   257→            <span class=\"date\">2026-05-13</span>\n   258→            <nav>\n   259→                <a href=\"#new-products\">New Products</a>\n   260→                <a href=\"#whitelist-updates\">Updates</a>\n   261→                <a href=\"#insights\">Insights</a>\n   262→            </nav>\n   263→        </div>\n   264→    </header>\n   265→\n   266→    <div class=\"container\">\n   267→        <main class=\"three-column-layout\">\n   268→            <!-- New Products Section -->\n   269→            <section class=\"column\" id=\"new-products\">\n   270→                <div class=\"column-header\">\n   271→                    New Products <span class=\"section-count\">(4)</span>\n   272→                </div>\n   273→                <div class=\"column-content\">\n   274→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   275→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   276→                            <a href=\"https://staff.rip\" target=\"_blank\">Staff.rip</a>\n   277→                        </div>\n   278→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   279→                            AI coding agent that lets teams describe code changes in plain language and ship them. Works across frontend, backend, microservices, and infra. Can be hosted or self-hosted with agent running locally so code never leaves machine.\n   280→                        </div>\n   281→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   282→                            <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n   283→                            <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   284→                            <span>2026-05-08</span>\n   285→                        </div>\n   286→                        <div class=\"quote\">\n   287→                            \"Giving the capability to ship to a broader audience, the way to empower codebases with the strength of the community\"\n   288→                        </div>\n   289→                    </div>\n   290→\n   291→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   292→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   293→                            <a href=\"https://bna.ahmedbna.com\" target=\"_blank\">BNA Code</a>\n   294→                        </div>\n   295→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   296→                            CLI AI agent that builds full-stack mobile apps from terminal. Choose stack (Expo React Native, Swift, Kotlin), describe app idea, and BNA launches frontend and backend agents to build mobile apps with authentication, realtime database, APIs, and native device features.\n   297→                        </div>\n   298→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   299→                            <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   300→                            <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   301→                            <span>2026-05-06</span>\n   302→                        </div>\n   303→                        <div class=\"quote\">\n   304→                            \"Just one command in your terminal. Go grab a coffee ☕ and come back to a full-stack real mobile app in favorite stack with full ownership of code and no vendor lock-in.\"\n   305→                        </div>\n   306→                    </div>\n   307→\n   308→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   309→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   310→                            <a href=\"https://clawtick.com\" target=\"_blank\">ClawTick</a>\n   311→                        </div>\n   312→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   313→                            Cloud scheduler built specifically for AI agents. Schedule LangChain, CrewAI, or webhook tasks with one CLI command. Provides built-in monitoring, failure alerts, automatic retries, and execution logs without managing servers or cron infrastructure.\n   314→                        </div>\n   315→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   316→                            <span class=\"tag\">AI workflow orchestration</span>\n   317→                            <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   318→                            <span>2026-05-06</span>\n   319→                        </div>\n   320→                        <div class=\"quote\">\n   321→                            \"CLI for agents, dashboard for humans is the cleanest way to position this — the moment scheduling has to happen, you want CLI; the moment you want to know what fired and what failed, you want UI.\"\n   322→                        </div>\n   323→                    </div>\n   324→\n   325→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   326→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   327→                            <a href=\"https://www.wozcode.com\" target=\"_blank\">WOZCODE</a>\n   328→                        </div>\n   329→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   330→                            Efficiency layer plugin for Claude Code that reduces token costs by up to 50% and improves performance. Replaces Claude's native tools with WozSearch and WozEdit for more efficient context handling. Official Anthropic-approved plugin.\n   331→                        </div>\n   332→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   333→                            <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   334→                            <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   335→                            <span>2026-05-01</span>\n   336→                        </div>\n   337→                        <div class=\"quote\">\n   338→                            \"In vanilla Claude Code, a simple 'find and edit 3 files' takes 12+ calls. WOZCODE collapses that to 2 calls. Context stays small, so every step that follows is cheaper and faster.\"\n   339→                        </div>\n   340→                    </div>\n   341→                </div>\n   342→            </section>\n   343→\n   344→            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section -->\n   345→            <section class=\"column\" id=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   346→                <div class=\"column-header\">\n   347→                    Whitelist Updates <span class=\"section-count\">(11)</span>\n   348→                </div>\n   349→                <div class=\"column-content\">\n   350→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   351→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   352→                            <span class=\"update-type announcement\">Claude Code</span>\n   353→                        </div>\n   354→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   355→                            Market Dominance and $30B ARR Achievement\n   356→                        </div>\n   357→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   358→                            As of May 2026, Claude Code has become the most-used AI coding tool, overtaking GitHub Copilot and Cursor in just eight months. Anthropic disclosed $30B ARR with 80x year-over-year growth.\n   359→                        </div>\n   360→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   361→                            <a href=\"https://dev.to/alexmercedcoder/ai-weekly-claude-code-dominates-mcp-goes-mainstream-week-of-march-5-2026-15af\" target=\"_blank\">Read more</a>\n   362→                            <span>2026-05-08</span>\n   363→                        </div>\n   364→                    </div>\n   365→\n   366→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   367→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   368→                            <span class=\"update-type release\">Devin</span>\n   369→                        </div>\n   370→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   371→                            May 2026 Updates\n   372→                        </div>\n   373→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   374→                            Enterprise features including sensitive toggle for secrets, merged multi-edits in progress tab, session category/subcategory in v3 API, wide markdown tables, SSO connection picker, and MCP OAuth token expiry warnings.\n   375→                        </div>\n   376→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   377→                            <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/2026\" target=\"_blank\">Release notes</a>\n   378→                            <span>2026-05-10</span>\n   379→                        </div>\n   380→                    </div>\n   381→\n   382→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   383→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   384→                            <span class=\"update-type release\">Gemini CLI</span>\n   385→                        </div>\n   386→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   387→                            v0.41.0 - Real-time Voice Mode\n   388→                        </div>\n   389→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   390→                            Real-time voice mode with cloud and local processing backends. Secure .env loading with workspace trust, stronger shell command capabilities, and bug fixes.\n   391→                        </div>\n   392→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   393→                            <a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\" target=\"_blank\">Changelog</a>\n   394→                            <span>2026-05-05</span>\n   395→                        </div>\n   396→                    </div>\n   397→\n   398→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   399→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   400→                            <span class=\"update-type feature\">Aider</span>\n   401→                        </div>\n   402→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   403→                            Claude 4.5/4.6 and Gemini 3 Support\n   404→                        </div>\n   405→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   406→                            Main branch now supports Claude 4.5/4.6 models with updated aliases. Expanded Gemini support includes 2.5 Flash and Flash-Lite, plus Gemini 3 preview models. Added DeepSeek Reasoner support.\n   407→                        </div>\n   408→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   409→                            <a href=\"https://aider.chat/HISTORY.html\" target=\"_blank\">History</a>\n   410→                            <span>2026-05-01</span>\n   411→                        </div>\n   412→                    </div>\n   413→\n   414→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   415→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   416→                            <span class=\"update-type feature\">Devin</span>\n   417→                        </div>\n   418→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   419→                            MCP Marketplace and Theme Selector\n   420→                        </div>\n   421→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   422→                            Added Datadog and Amplitude to MCP marketplace as remote servers with OAuth. Theme selector now generally available. Wiki v2 uses stronger reasoning with subagents.\n   423→                        </div>\n   424→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   425→                            <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/2026\" target=\"_blank\">Release notes</a>\n   426→                            <span>2026-04-25</span>\n   427→                        </div>\n   428→                    </div>\n   429→\n   430→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   431→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   432→                            <span class=\"update-type feature\">Cursor</span>\n   433→                        </div>\n   434→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   435→                            Microsoft Teams Integration\n   436→                        </div>\n   437→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   438→                            Now available in Microsoft Teams - mention @Cursor to delegate tasks. Teams admins can customize Bugbot effort levels. New PR review experience and Build in Parallel feature.\n   439→                        </div>\n   440→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   441→                            <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Changelog</a>\n   442→                            <span>2026-04-20</span>\n   443→                        </div>\n   444→                    </div>\n   445→\n   446→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   447→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   448→                            <span class=\"update-type release\">Aider</span>\n   449→                        </div>\n   450→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   451→                            v0.86.0 - GPT-5 and Grok-4 Support\n   452→                        </div>\n   453→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   454→                            Expands GPT-5 model support across family variants and providers including dated and chat/mini/nano variants. Aider wrote 88% of the code in this release.\n   455→                        </div>\n   456→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   457→                            <a href=\"https://aider.chat/HISTORY.html\" target=\"_blank\">Release notes</a>\n   458→                            <span>2026-04-20</span>\n   459→                        </div>\n   460→                    </div>\n   461→\n   462→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   463→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   464→                            <span class=\"update-type feature\">Cursor</span>\n   465→                        </div>\n   466→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   467→                            Enterprise Model Controls\n   468→                        </div>\n   469→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   470→                            Enterprise admins can set granular model access controls at provider and model level, with option to block new providers/versions by default. Soft spend limits and intelligent alerts.\n   471→                        </div>\n   472→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   473→                            <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Changelog</a>\n   474→                            <span>2026-04-10</span>\n   475→                        </div>\n   476→                    </div>\n   477→\n   478→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   479→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   480→                            <span class=\"update-type release\">Gemini CLI</span>\n   481→                        </div>\n   482→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   483→                            v0.40.0 - Offline Search\n   484→                        </div>\n   485→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   486→                            Bundled ripgrep for offline search support and GitHub-style colorblind themes. MCP resource tools and prompt-driven four-tier memory management system.\n   487→                        </div>\n   488→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   489→                            <a href=\"https://geminicli.com/docs/changelogs/\" target=\"_blank\">Changelog</a>\n   490→                            <span>2026-04-28</span>\n   491→                        </div>\n   492→                    </div>\n   493→\n   494→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   495→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   496→                            <span class=\"update-type release\">Aider</span>\n   497→                        </div>\n   498→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   499→                            v0.85.0 - Gemini 2.5 Models\n   500→                        </div>\n   501→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   502→                            Adds support for gemini-2.5-pro, gemini-2.5-flash, and gemini-2.5-pro-preview-06-05 with thinking tokens. Updated model aliases and o3-pro support across providers.\n   503→                        </div>\n   504→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   505→                            <a href=\"https://aider.chat/HISTORY.html\" target=\"_blank\">Release notes</a>\n   506→                            <span>2026-04-08</span>\n   507→                        </div>\n   508→                    </div>\n   509→\n   510→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   511→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   512→                            <span class=\"update-type release\">Devin</span>\n   513→                        </div>\n   514→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   515→                            Devin 2.2 - 3x Faster Startup\n   516→                        </div>\n   517→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   518→                            3x faster startup time, new UI connecting entire dev lifecycle, and smoother Slack/Linear integrations. Full desktop testing capability with computer control on Linux apps.\n   519→                        </div>\n   520→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   521→                            <a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/release-notes/2026\" target=\"_blank\">Release notes</a>\n   522→                            <span>2026-04-15</span>\n   523→                        </div>\n   524→                    </div>\n   525→                </div>\n   526→            </section>\n   527→\n   528→            <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n   529→            <section class=\"column\" id=\"insights\">\n   530→                <div class=\"column-header\">\n   531→                    Technical Insights <span class=\"section-count\">(14)</span>\n   532→                </div>\n   533→                <div class=\"column-content\">\n   534→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   535→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   536→                            <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40812345\" target=\"_blank\">Show HN: Needle</a>\n   537→                        </div>\n   538→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   539→                            Gemini Tool Calling distilled to 26M model - showing how expensive AI capabilities can be compressed for edge deployment.\n   540→                        </div>\n   541→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   542→                            <span class=\"tag\">model-distillation</span>\n   543→                            <span class=\"tag\">tool-calling</span>\n   544→                        </div>\n   545→                        <div class=\"topics\">\n   546→                            <span class=\"tag\">edge-ai</span>\n   547→                            <span class=\"tag\">optimization</span>\n   548→                        </div>\n   549→                    </div>\n   550→\n   551→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   552→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   553→                            <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40812890\" target=\"_blank\">Agentic interface for mainframes</a>\n   554→                        </div>\n   555→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   556→                            AI-powered interface making mainframe and COBOL systems accessible through agentic AI, addressing legacy system maintenance skills gap.\n   557→                        </div>\n   558→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   559→                            <span class=\"tag\">cobol</span>\n   560→                            <span class=\"tag\">mainframes</span>\n   561→                        </div>\n   562→                        <div class=\"topics\">\n   563→                            <span class=\"tag\">ai-agents</span>\n   564→                            <span class=\"tag\">legacy-systems</span>\n   565→                        </div>\n   566→                    </div>\n   567→\n   568→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   569→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   570→                            <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40812945\" target=\"_blank\">Statewright: Visual state machines</a>\n   571→                        </div>\n   572→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   573→                            Visual state machine framework making AI agents more reliable through structured state management, addressing reliability challenges.\n   574→                        </div>\n   575→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   576→                            <span class=\"tag\">ai-agents</span>\n   577→                            <span class=\"tag\">state-machines</span>\n   578→                        </div>\n   579→                        <div class=\"topics\">\n   580→                            <span class=\"tag\">reliability</span>\n   581→                            <span class=\"tag\">visual-programming</span>\n   582→                        </div>\n   583→                    </div>\n   584→\n   585→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   586→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   587→                            <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40813456\" target=\"_blank\">Launch HN: Voker (YC S24)</a>\n   588→                        </div>\n   589→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   590→                            Analytics and observability tools specifically for AI agent systems, reflecting growing need for monitoring and debugging tools.\n   591→                        </div>\n   592→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   593→                            <span class=\"tag\">ai-agents</span>\n   594→                            <span class=\"tag\">analytics</span>\n   595→                        </div>\n   596→                        <div class=\"topics\">\n   597→                            <span class=\"tag\">observability</span>\n   598→                            <span class=\"tag\">yc</span>\n   599→                        </div>\n   600→                    </div>\n   601→\n   602→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   603→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   604→                            <a href=\"https://tanstack.com/blog/changelog/npm-postmortem\" target=\"_blank\">TanStack NPM supply-chain compromise</a>\n   605→                        </div>\n   606→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   607→                            Detailed postmortem of supply-chain attack on popular TanStack library, highlighting npm security challenges and package integrity importance.\n   608→                        </div>\n   609→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   610→                            <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n   611→                            <span class=\"tag\">supply-chain</span>\n   612→                        </div>\n   613→                        <div class=\"topics\">\n   614→                            <span class=\"tag\">npm</span>\n   615→                            <span class=\"tag\">postmortem</span>\n   616→                        </div>\n   617→                    </div>\n   618→\n   619→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   620→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   621→                            <a href=\"https://x.com/karpathy/status/2004607146781278521\" target=\"_blank\">Karpathy: 'I've never felt this much behind'</a>\n   622→                        </div>\n   623→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   624→                            At Sequoia AI Ascent 2026, Karpathy reflected on programming being dramatically refactored by AI, expressing feeling more behind than ever.\n   625→                        </div>\n   626→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   627→                            <span class=\"tag\">ai-coding</span>\n   628→                            <span class=\"tag\">vibe-coding</span>\n   629→                        </div>\n   630→                        <div class=\"topics\">\n   631→                            <span class=\"tag\">karpathy</span>\n   632→                            <span class=\"tag\">opinion</span>\n   633→                        </div>\n   634→                    </div>\n   635→\n   636→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   637→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   638→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/10/nyt-hallucination/\" target=\"_blank\">NYT AI Hallucination Correction</a>\n   639→                        </div>\n   640→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   641→                            NYT issued editors' note after AI-generated summary was incorrectly rendered as direct quotation, highlighting risks in journalism without verification.\n   642→                        </div>\n   643→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   644→                            <span class=\"tag\">ai-ethics</span>\n   645→                            <span class=\"tag\">hallucinations</span>\n   646→                        </div>\n   647→                        <div class=\"topics\">\n   648→                            <span class=\"tag\">journalism</span>\n   649→                            <span class=\"tag\">generative-ai</span>\n   650→                        </div>\n   651→                    </div>\n   652→\n   653→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   654→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   655→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/9/webrtc-openai/\" target=\"_blank\">OpenAI's WebRTC Problem with Voice AI</a>\n   656→                        </div>\n   657→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   658→                            WebRTC aggressively drops audio packets for low latency, but for LLM voice apps where users are \"paying to boil the ocean,\" accurate transmission matters more than 200ms savings.\n   659→                        </div>\n   660→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   661→                            <span class=\"tag\">webrtc</span>\n   662→                            <span class=\"tag\">openai</span>\n   663→                        </div>\n   664→                        <div class=\"topics\">\n   665→                            <span class=\"tag\">voice-ai</span>\n   666→                            <span class=\"tag\">latency</span>\n   667→                        </div>\n   668→                    </div>\n   669→\n   670→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   671→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   672→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/8/html/\" target=\"_blank\">Using Claude Code: HTML Effectiveness</a>\n   673→                        </div>\n   674→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   675→                            Thariq Shihipar advocates for HTML over Markdown - allows SVG diagrams, interactive widgets, in-page navigation, and rich styling for LLM outputs.\n   676→                        </div>\n   677→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   678→                            <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n   679→                            <span class=\"tag\">html</span>\n   680→                        </div>\n   681→                        <div class=\"topics\">\n   682→                            <span class=\"tag\">prompt-engineering</span>\n   683→                            <span class=\"tag\">llms</span>\n   684→                        </div>\n   685→                    </div>\n   686→\n   687→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   688→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   689→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/7/firefox-claude-mythos/\" target=\"_blank\">Hardening Firefox with Claude Mythos</a>\n   690→                        </div>\n   691→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   692→                            Mozilla used Claude Mythos preview to find and fix hundreds of Firefox vulnerabilities. Firefox went from fixing 20-30 bugs/month to 423 in April 2026.\n   693→                        </div>\n   694→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   695→                            <span class=\"tag\">mozilla</span>\n   696→                            <span class=\"tag\">firefox</span>\n   697→                        </div>\n   698→                        <div class=\"topics\">\n   699→                            <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n   700→                            <span class=\"tag\">claude</span>\n   701→                        </div>\n   702→                    </div>\n   703→\n   704→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   705→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   706→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/7/xai-anthropic-data-center/\" target=\"_blank\">xAI/Anthropic data center deal</a>\n   707→                        </div>\n   708→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   709→                            Anthropic struck deal with SpaceX/xAI to use \"all of the capacity of their Colossus data center\" - one of biggest announcements at Code w/ Claude 2026.\n   710→                        </div>\n   711→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   712→                            <span class=\"tag\">anthropic</span>\n   713→                            <span class=\"tag\">xai</span>\n   714→                        </div>\n   715→                        <div class=\"topics\">\n   716→                            <span class=\"tag\">data-centers</span>\n   717→                            <span class=\"tag\">scaling</span>\n   718→                        </div>\n   719→                    </div>\n   720→\n   721→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   722→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   723→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/6/code-w-claude-2026/\" target=\"_blank\">Live blog: Code w/ Claude 2026</a>\n   724→                        </div>\n   725→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   726→                            Major announcements: Claude Code rate limits doubling, 17x YoY API volume increase, Claude Managed Agents, Claude Desktop app, and customer stories from Shopify and Mercado Libre.\n   727→                        </div>\n   728→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   729→                            <span class=\"tag\">anthropic</span>\n   730→                            <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n   731→                        </div>\n   732→                        <div class=\"topics\">\n   733→                            <span class=\"tag\">ai-coding</span>\n   734→                            <span class=\"tag\">enterprise-ai</span>\n   735→                        </div>\n   736→                    </div>\n   737→\n   738→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   739→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   740→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/6/vibe-coding-agentic-engineering/\" target=\"_blank\">Vibe coding and agentic engineering</a>\n   741→                        </div>\n   742→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   743→                            Simon Willison explores convergence of \"vibe coding\" (iterative experimentation) and \"agentic engineering\" (systematic AI-driven development) raising questions about future of software development.\n   744→                        </div>\n   745→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   746→                            <span class=\"tag\">vibe-coding</span>\n   747→                            <span class=\"tag\">agentic-engineering</span>\n   748→                        </div>\n   749→                        <div class=\"topics\">\n   750→                            <span class=\"tag\">ai-coding</span>\n   751→                            <span class=\"tag\">philosophy</span>\n   752→                        </div>\n   753→                    </div>\n   754→\n   755→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   756→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   757→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/6/redis-arrays/\" target=\"_blank\">Redis Arrays: New Data Type</a>\n   758→                        </div>\n   759→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   760→                            antirez proposed adding new \"array\" data type to Redis with 21 new commands including ARGREP for server-side grep using TRE regex library.\n   761→                        </div>\n   762→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   763→                            <span class=\"tag\">redis</span>\n   764→                            <span class=\"tag\">databases</span>\n   765→                        </div>\n   766→                        <div class=\"topics\">\n   767→                            <span class=\"tag\">claude-code</span>\n   768→                            <span class=\"tag\">wasm</span>\n   769→                        </div>\n   770→                    </div>\n   771→                </div>\n   772→            </section>\n   773→        </main>\n   774→    </div>\n   775→\n   776→    <footer class=\"footer\">\n   777→        <a href=\"#top\">Back to top</a>\n   778→        <span>|</span>\n   779→        <a href=\"https://github.com/agentdaily/agentdaily\" target=\"_blank\">GitHub</a>\n   780→        <span>|</span>\n   781→        <span>Generated: 2026-05-13</span>\n   782→    </footer>\n   783→</body>\n   784→</html>\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"
