      }\n   259→\n   260→            .technical-insights {\n   261→                grid-column: 1 / -1;\n   262→            }\n   263→        }\n   264→\n   265→        @media (max-width: 768px) {\n   266→            .three-column-layout {\n   267→                grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n   268→            }\n   269→\n   270→            body {\n   271→                font-size: 11pt;\n   272→            }\n   273→        }\n   274→\n   275→        @media print {\n   276→            body {\n   277→                background-color: #ffffff;\n   278→            }\n   279→\n   280→            .column {\n   281→                border: 1px solid #000000;\n   282→                page-break-inside: avoid;\n   283→            }\n   284→\n   285→            .column-header {\n   286→                background-color: #eeeeee !important;\n   287→                -webkit-print-color-adjust: exact;\n   288→                print-color-adjust: exact;\n   289→            }\n   290→\n   291→            a {\n   292→                color: #000000 !important;\n   293→                text-decoration: underline;\n   294→            }\n   295→\n   296→            .item {\n   297→                page-break-inside: avoid;\n   298→            }\n   299→        }\n   300→    </style>\n   301→</head>\n   302→<body>\n   303→    <header class=\"header\">\n   304→        <div class=\"header-content\">\n   305→            <h1>Agentic Coding Daily Report</h1>\n   306→            <span class=\"date\">May 13, 2026</span>\n   307→            <nav>\n   308→                <a href=\"#new-products\">New Products</a>\n   309→                <a href=\"#whitelist-updates\">Updates</a>\n   310→                <a href=\"#insights\">Insights</a>\n   311→            </nav>\n   312→        </div>\n   313→    </header>\n   314→\n   315→    <div class=\"container\">\n   316→        <main class=\"three-column-layout\">\n   317→            <!-- New Products Section -->\n   318→            <section class=\"column\" id=\"new-products\">\n   319→                <div class=\"column-header\">\n   320→                    New Products <span class=\"section-count\">(5)</span>\n   321→                </div>\n   322→                <div class=\"column-content\">\n   323→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   324→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   325→                            <a href=\"https://github.com/av/mi\" target=\"_blank\">Mi</a>\n   326→                        </div>\n   327→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   328→                            30-line zero-config CLI agent for bug fixes and refactoring. Autonomous coding agent that fits in a single JavaScript file with no framework or dependencies beyond Node builtins. Works with any OpenAI-compatible API.\n   329→                        </div>\n   330→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   331→                            <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   332→                            <span class=\"tag\">GitHub</span>\n   333→                            <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-12</span>\n   334→                        </div>\n   335→                        <div class=\"quote\">\n   336→                            \"how small can an agentic harness be and remain useful? turns out, very small. Claude Code is ~500k lines of code, OpenCode is ~100k, mi is 30 lines, yet, it has all the features expected from agentic harness\"\n   337→                        </div>\n   338→                    </div>\n   339→\n   340→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   341→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   342→                            <a href=\"https://github.com/linchpinhq/linchpin\" target=\"_blank\">Linchpin</a>\n   343→                        </div>\n   344→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   345→                            Open-source, self-hostable runtime for managed AI agents under Apache-2.0 license. Deploy with single 'docker compose up' command to get a full agent platform with REST + SSE API, per-session Docker sandbox, MCP tools, encrypted vaults.\n   346→                        </div>\n   347→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   348→                            <span class=\"tag\">code agent infrastructure</span>\n   349→                            <span class=\"tag\">GitHub</span>\n   350→                            <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-12</span>\n   351→                        </div>\n   352→                        <div class=\"quote\">\n   353→                            \"Every time Devin, Manus, or Operator launched, the top comment on HN was some variant of 'is this open source?' The answer kept being no. So we built Linchpin.\"\n   354→                        </div>\n   355→                    </div>\n   356→\n   357→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   358→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   359→                            <a href=\"https://github.com/aaronkwhite/bosshogg-cli\" target=\"_blank\">BossHogg</a>\n   360→                        </div>\n   361→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   362→                            Agent-first CLI for PostHog analytics and feature flags. Gives AI coding agents a compact, scriptable way to operate PostHog without loading a large MCP tool surface. Supports HogQL queries and production-safe analytics operations.\n   363→                        </div>\n   364→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   365→                            <span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span>\n   366→                            <span class=\"tag\">GitHub</span>\n   367→                            <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-12</span>\n   368→                        </div>\n   369→                        <div class=\"quote\">\n   370→                            \"MCPs have a purpose. CLIs have a purpose. PostHog MCP is great for rich assistant workflows... But when you are working inside Claude Code, Cursor, scripts, or CI, you often want something smaller and more deterministic\"\n   371→                        </div>\n   372→                    </div>\n   373→\n   374→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   375→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   376→                            <a href=\"https://xyops.io\" target=\"_blank\">xyOps</a>\n   377→                        </div>\n   378→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   379→                            Open-source operations automation platform for self-hosted teams under BSD-3-Clause license. Schedule jobs, build visual workflows, monitor servers, trigger alerts. Full app feature set is open source - no enterprise fork.\n   380→                        </div>\n   381→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   382→                            <span class=\"tag\">workflow agent</span>\n   383→                            <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   384→                            <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-09</span>\n   385→                        </div>\n   386→                        <div class=\"quote\">\n   387→                            \"The full app is open source under BSD-3-Clause. There is no separate enterprise fork, no hidden feature set, no license key, and no telemetry.\"\n   388→                        </div>\n   389→                    </div>\n   390→\n   391→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   392→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   393→                            <a href=\"https://mycelis.ai\" target=\"_blank\">Mycelis</a>\n   394→                        </div>\n   395→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   396→                            Serverless AI workspace with smart routing and MCP agents. Abstracts hardware completely - instantly spin up open-source models on optimized GPUs or bring your own keys. Features conditional smart routing to optimal models.\n   397→                        </div>\n   398→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   399→                            <span class=\"tag\">AI infrastructure</span>\n   400→                            <span class=\"tag\">Product Hunt</span>\n   401→                            <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-12</span>\n   402→                        </div>\n   403→                        <div class=\"quote\">\n   404→                            \"routing specific tasks to the most optimal model is the absolute best way forward\"\n   405→                        </div>\n   406→                    </div>\n   407→                </div>\n   408→            </section>\n   409→\n   410→            <!-- Whitelist Updates Section -->\n   411→            <section class=\"column\" id=\"whitelist-updates\">\n   412→                <div class=\"column-header\">\n   413→                    Product Updates <span class=\"section-count\">(11)</span>\n   414→                </div>\n   415→                <div class=\"column-content\">\n   416→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   417→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   418→                            <span class=\"update-type release\">Claude Code</span>\n   419→                        </div>\n   420→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   421→                            v2.1.140 - Enhanced Agent Tool Matching\n   422→                        </div>\n   423→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   424→                            Improves agent tool subagent_type matching with case- and separator-insensitive values. Fixed /goal hanging with disableAllHooks, resolved settings hot-reload issues with symlinked files.\n   425→                        </div>\n   426→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   427→                            <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Changelog</a>\n   428→                            <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-12</span>\n   429→                        </div>\n   430→                    </div>\n   431→\n   432→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   433→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   434→                            <span class=\"update-type feature\">Claude Code</span>\n   435→                        </div>\n   436→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   437→                            v2.1.139 - Agent View and /goal Command\n   438→                        </div>\n   439→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   440→                            Adds agent view (Research Preview) showing all Claude Code sessions. Introduced /goal command to set completion conditions with live elapsed/turns/tokens overlay. Added /scroll-speed command.\n   441→                        </div>\n   442→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   443→                            <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/changelog\" target=\"_blank\">Changelog</a>\n   444→                            <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-11</span>\n   445→                        </div>\n   446→                    </div>\n   447→\n   448→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   449→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   450→                            <span class=\"update-type feature\">Devin</span>\n   451→                        </div>\n   452→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   453→                            May 2026 Updates - Enterprise Features\n   454→                        </div>\n   455→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   456→                            Sensitive toggle for secrets with mask/visible options, merged multi-edits in progress tab, session category/subcategory in v3 API, wide markdown tables in chat, SSO connection picker.\n   457→                      