tem-title\">\n   671→                            <a href=\"https://tanstack.com/blog/changelog/npm-postmortem\" target=\"_blank\">TanStack NPM supply-chain compromise</a>\n   672→                        </div>\n   673→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   674→                            Detailed postmortem of supply-chain attack on popular TanStack library, highlighting npm security challenges and package integrity importance.\n   675→                        </div>\n   676→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   677→                            <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-12</span>\n   678→                        </div>\n   679→                        <div class=\"topics\">\n   680→                            <span class=\"tag\">security</span>\n   681→                            <span class=\"tag\">supply-chain</span>\n   682→                        </div>\n   683→                    </div>\n   684→\n   685→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   686→                        <div class=\"insight-type opinion\">OPINION</div>\n   687→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   688→                            <a href=\"https://x.com/karpathy/status/2004607146781278521\" target=\"_blank\">Karpathy: 'Never felt this much behind'</a>\n   689→                        </div>\n   690→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   691→                            At Sequoia AI Ascent 2026, Karpathy reflected on programming being dramatically refactored by AI, expressing feeling more behind than ever.\n   692→                        </div>\n   693→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   694→                            <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-10</span>\n   695→                        </div>\n   696→                        <div class=\"topics\">\n   697→                            <span class=\"tag\">ai-coding</span>\n   698→                            <span class=\"tag\">vibe-coding</span>\n   699→                        </div>\n   700→                    </div>\n   701→\n   702→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   703→                        <div class=\"insight-type discussion\">DISCUSSION</div>\n   704→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   705→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/10/nyt-hallucination/\" target=\"_blank\">NYT AI Hallucination Correction</a>\n   706→                        </div>\n   707→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   708→                            NYT issued editors' note after AI-generated summary was incorrectly rendered as direct quotation, highlighting risks in journalism without verification.\n   709→                        </div>\n   710→                        <div class=\"item-meta\">\n   711→                            <span class=\"date-badge\">2026-05-10</span>\n   712→                        </div>\n   713→                        <div class=\"topics\">\n   714→                            <span class=\"tag\">ai-ethics</span>\n   715→                            <span class=\"tag\">hallucinations</span>\n   716→                        </div>\n   717→                    </div>\n   718→\n   719→                    <div class=\"item\">\n   720→                        <div class=\"insight-type technical\">TECHNICAL</div>\n   721→                        <div class=\"item-title\">\n   722→                            <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/9/webrtc-openai/\" target=\"_blank\">OpenAI's WebRTC Problem with Voice AI</a>\n   723→                        </div>\n   724→                        <div class=\"item-description\">\n   725→                            WebRTC aggressively drops audio packets for low latency, but for LLM voice apps where users are \"paying to boil the ocean,\" accurate transmission matters more than 200ms savings.\n   726→                        </div>\n   727→                        <div class